From 7129ddb93dbc5e166f369c7fb370520404dc5000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Velox <velox@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:54:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gfxstream: fence status hints and a sync wait deadlock fix

Host:
- GOLDFISH_SYNC_VULKAN_FENCE_HINT (0x56 in the low byte of the sync
  device thread handle, the fence's submission number above it): signal
  the guest sync fd once that submission completed, was reset after it,
  was superseded by another submission, or the fence was destroyed.
  The wait re-checks every 2 ms, so a request that arrives after a
  reset never holds one of the four sync workers.
- FenceInfo counts submissions and resets.
- Fix a lock order inversion: waitForFences(checkWaitState) took
  mMutex inside the condition variable predicate while holding the
  fence mutex, while on_vkQueueSubmit takes mMutex and then the fence
  mutex. Fence state writes (including resets) now hold the fence
  mutex, and the predicate no longer takes mMutex.
- Advertise ANDROID_EMU_vulkan_fence_status_hint.

Guest: query the capability and pass it to the Vulkan driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I846b41c75b35944973f5938cf46c259b637191df
